# Text is stored with LF and checked out with LF on every OS, so Prettier (endOfLine "lf"), the
# shell scripts and the generated docs agree on Windows too. Before, Windows checkouts followed
# core.autocrlf and `prettier --write` rewrote every CRLF file it touched.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.zip binary
*.pdf binary
